## Why this resolves the finding
The reviewer's line was `E2E-001: not measurable`: no step named a
criterion a run could settle. The new Then step names the exact message
`"Hello, <name>!"`, a verbatim string a step definition can assert on,
so the check now reads `E2E-001: measurable — '"Hello, <name>!"'`. The
behaviour is unchanged: greeting the person whose name the greeter is
given is exactly printing `Hello, <name>!` with that name, and `<name>`
still refers to the name the When step supplies.

